Mojang does multiple complex raytraces to deal with/stop players from hitting targets behind walls with the spear. They raytrace to the center of the target entity and if that raytrace is blocked by say a block they make the crosshair target empty.

LightningGrim on the other hand is given need even more reworking than it already does to deal with supporting hitting through walls with the spear.

If we really wanted to flag this the pseduocode would look something like
```java
public boolean validateHit(GrimPlayer attacker, PacketEntity target, Vector3d hitPos, ItemStack stack) {
    // 1. Standard LOS Check (Always Required)
    // Raycast from eyes to the point they claimed they hit
    if (RayTrace.hasBlocks(attacker.getEyePos(), hitPos)) {
        return false; // Hit through a wall (Standard)
    }

    // 2. The New Margin Check (Conditional)
    double margin = getHitboxMargin(stack);
    if (margin > 0) {
        SimpleCollisionBox realBox = target.getPossibleCollisionBoxes();
        
        // If the hit point is OUTSIDE the real box (meaning they hit the margin/air)
        if (!realBox.isVecInside(hitPos)) {
            // Perform the Mojank wall check
            // Raycast from HitPos -> Target Center
            if (RayTrace.hasBlocks(hitPos, realBox.getCenter())) {
                return false; // Margin wallbang detected
            }
        }
    }

    return true;
}
```

To prevent abusing this the margin to hit entities behind walls, but that's a very minor bypass for something that only LightningGrim currently tries to stop and not perfectly.

